# Kotlin/Android security

Narrows `core-common-rules`' security rules to Android risks in OWASP Mobile Top 10.

## Secrets and credential storage

- Never store a credential, auth token or API secret in plain `SharedPreferences`.
  For new code prefer the Android Keystore directly (store the key there, encrypt
  the value yourself) over `EncryptedSharedPreferences`
  (`androidx.security:security-crypto`), which Google no longer recommends for new
  applications; check its current status in the Android docs before using it in a
  codebase that already depends on it.
- Never hard-code an API key, client secret or signing credential as a Kotlin
  string literal or a `BuildConfig` field, committed or injected at build time
  from `local.properties` or a CI secret: `BuildConfig` is compiled into the APK.
  A value that must stay off the device is fetched from a backend at runtime.
- Generate and store cryptographic keys through `AndroidKeyStore`
  (`KeyGenParameterSpec`), not derived or hard-coded in application code.

## Manifest and component exposure

- Every `<activity>`, `<service>`, `<receiver>` and `<provider>` not meant to be
  reachable from other apps has `android:exported="false"` (or no `exported`
  attribute and no intent-filter).
- An exported component that must stay exported (deep-link entry, share target)
  validates every piece of the incoming `Intent` before acting on it.
- Guard a `ContentProvider` and any exported component with a signature-level
  custom permission when the caller is meant to be your own other app.

## Secure intent and deep-link handling

- Treat every value from an incoming `Intent` (extras, deep-link segments and
  query params, share `ClipData`) as untrusted: validate shape and range before
  using it to navigate, query a database or build a file path.
- Prefer an explicit `Intent` within your own app; use an implicit `Intent` only
  when another app must handle it, and set `setPackage` when only your own app
  should respond.
- Validate a deep-link's scheme/host/path against an allowlist before using any
  part of it; verified `https` App Links do not make a query parameter or path
  segment trusted.

## Data and transport

- Require TLS for every network call carrying credentials or personal data; no
  custom `TrustManager`/`HostnameVerifier` that accepts all certificates outside
  a short-lived local debug build, and never shipped.
- Mark a view/field that must not appear in screenshots or the app-switcher
  preview (PIN entry, payment details) with `FLAG_SECURE`.
- No PII, tokens or full request/response bodies in `Log.d`/`Log.i` in release
  builds; gate verbose logging behind a debug-only flag.
